  "_peripherals": [
    "Per-board peripheral capability, consulted by the C++ -> C translator.",
    "  hardware  the silicon has the peripheral",
    "  software  no peripheral, but NiusBurner ships a bit-banged runtime",
    "  none      neither; the translator refuses APIs that need it rather",
    "            than emitting something that silently changes timing",
    "A classic 8051 has no TWI, no SPI unit, no PWM and no ADC. Two-wire and",
    "three-wire buses are bit-banged, which is why they are 'software'; PWM",
    "and ADC cannot be faked without stealing a timer or an external part, so",
    "they stay 'none'."
  ]
